# Testing (Node.js)

## TDD

- Red/Green/Refactor; write failing test first; minimal code to pass; refactor with tests green

## Unit Tests (Vitest)

- **Setup:** Vitest with Node environment; path aliases; setupFiles for global mocks and env
- **Structure:** Describe/it; Arrange-Act-Assert; mock external deps (vi.mock)
- **Naming:** should {expected} when {condition}
- **Coverage:** Exclude node_modules, types, test files; aim for critical paths

## API Tests (Supertest)

- Request app (Express/Fastify) with supertest; assert status, body, headers; use factories for test data
- Test auth (valid/invalid token), validation (400), not found (404), success (200/201)

## Integration (Testcontainers)

- Spin up Postgres, Redis, etc. in containers; run migrations; run tests against real DB; tear down
- Use for repository and integration tests; keep fast with single container or shared setup

## Mocking

- **HTTP:** Mock fetch or axios; or use MSW
- **DB:** Use test DB (Testcontainers) or in-memory when appropriate
- **Time:** vi.useFakeTimers for time-sensitive tests

## Conventions

- Fast unit tests; integration tests for boundaries; no production secrets; deterministic tests

## Anti-Patterns

- Testing implementation details; flaky tests; no cleanup; real external calls in unit tests

